{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And Melchizedek king of Shalem</b> — this is Jerusalem, as it is said (Psalms 76:3), \"And His tabernacle was in Shalem,\" and its king was also called in the days of Joshua \"Adoni-zedek\" (Joshua 10:1), for ever since the nations knew that that place was the choicest of places in the middle of the inhabited world, or they knew its excellence by tradition that it is aligned opposite the heavenly Temple above, where the Shekhinah of the Holy One, blessed be He, resides — He being called \"Tzedek.\" And in Bereshit Rabbah (43:6): this place vindicates (מצדיק) its inhabitants, and [therefore the names] Melchizedek, Adoni-zedek; Jerusalem is called Tzedek, as it is said (Isaiah 1:21), \"Righteousness (צדק) lodged in her.\"" "And he mentioned <b>and he was priest to El Elyon</b> to make known that Abraham would not give tithe to a priest of other elohim, but because he knew of him that he was a priest to El Elyon, he gave him the tithe for the honor of HaShem. And this was a hint to Abraham that there the House of Elohim would be, and there his offspring would set forth the tithe and the terumah, and there they would bless HaShem. And according to the opinion of our Sages (Nedarim 32b), who say that Melchizedek was Shem son of Noah — he went from his land to Jerusalem to serve HaShem there, and he served them as priest to El Elyon, for he was the honored brother of their father, since Jerusalem is from the territory of the Canaanite from of old. And Rashi wrote above (Genesis 12:6) on \"And the Canaanite was then in the land\" — he [the Canaanite] was going and conquering the land of Israel from the seed of Shem, the forefather of Abraham, for in the portion of Shem it [the land] fell when Noah divided the earth among his sons (Sifra 126), as it is said, \"And Melchizedek king of Shalem.\" But this is not correct, for \"the border of the Canaanite was from Sidon\" (Genesis 10:19) includes all the land of Israel, and the border of the sons of Shem is in the east, far from the land of Israel. Rather, if Noah divided the lands among his sons and gave the land of Israel to Shem, that would be like \"one who divides his property by his own word [during his lifetime]\" (i.e., a non-binding gift), and the sons of Canaan dwelt in it until HaShem would bequeath it to the seed of His beloved, as I have already mentioned (Ramban on Genesis 10:15)." "<b>And he was priest to El Elyon</b> — because among all the nations there were priests ministering to the angels called \"elim,\" as it is said (Exodus 15:11), \"Who is like You among the elim,\" therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, is called \"El Elyon.\" And its meaning is: the mighty One who is exalted above all those who are exalted, as in \"It is in the power (אל) of my hand\" (Genesis 31:29). And Melchizedek did not mention the Name, but Abraham said, \"YHWH, El Elyon\" (Genesis 14:22)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:29:35.180488545Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}